{
 "id": "belt-tensioner-fdm",
 "brief": "A belt tensioner arm for my robot's base, PETG FDM, printed flat (layers along Z), 8 mm thick\n(z = -4 to 4). It swings on an M5 shoulder bolt along Z at the origin (5.2 mm hole, 4 mm of wall)\nand carries an idler pulley on an M5 axle 50 mm away at (50, 0), also a 5.2 mm hole with 4 mm of\nwall. A spring hooks into a 4 mm hole at (20, -15) (along Z, 3 mm of wall) and holds the arm\nstill. Fits in x = -10 to 60, y = -22 to 10. The belt wraps the idler and pulls it with\n2 x 40 N, the resultant points roughly toward +X+Y at 45 degrees (about 75 N). It runs for\nyears. Safety factor 2.",
